[C1] PASS the energy floor uses the already-floored density, so the two passes do not commute: reversing them changes the energy in 2862 of 3000 random states, by up to 1.33e+04 in absolute energy; a cell below the density floor gets a different minimum internal energy under each order
[C2] PASS the floors invent mass and energy; they are repairs, not conservative operations: on 4000 cells straddling the floors they add 4.736e-04 of dry mass and 1.294e+02 of total energy, both strictly positive: a clamp can only add. Nothing anywhere removes it again
[C3] PASS the condensate borrow conserves mass where a clamp to zero invents it: over 2000 cells with negative condensate, clamping to zero adds 3.770e-02 of mass while the borrow changes the total by 0.0e+00; 0 cells went vapour-negative and are left to the column repair
[C4] PASS a repair marks the block for a redo, and only from the interior: an untouched state marks nothing (False, False); a density below the floor sets the patch mark (True, False); a NaN sets the NaN mark (True, True); the same density repair outside the interior marks nothing (False, False)
[C5] PASS the primitive pass floors density and pressure and clamps species, and floors no temperature: density 1e-09 -> 1e-06, pressure 1e-09 -> 1e-03, a negative mass fraction -> 0e+00; an admissible cell is untouched. The conserved pass instead floors energy through a temperature floor of 20 K, which has no primitive counterpart
[C6] PASS the face-pressure fallback cannot fire at rest and is positive whenever it does: at rest the face pressure is the reference bit for bit in 200000 of 200000 faces and never non-positive, so the well-balanced state is untouched; with a perturbation the fallback fires at 23949 faces and the result is strictly positive at all 200000. The density fallback is the adjacent cell's value, chosen from a run rather than from theory, and is not checked here
[C7] PASS the redo detector tests a margin above the floor, so a nudged cell is still a hit: of 15 nudges of a just-floored cell the 1.001 margin counts all 15 as hits; equality with the floor counts only 2, the unnudged cell and the one nudge below machine epsilon. The 13 nudges from 1e-15 to 1e-03 relative are the hits the margin keeps and equality loses. A density 1.002 times the floor is a hit under neither test
[C8] PASS the borrow conserves the cell total because the parent fractions are normalised: over 2000 cells with 1 to 4 parents the total changes by at most 0.92 of eps_m/2 ((K + 1)|d| + sum of the parents); the same additions with the un-normalised weights nu mu change it by up to 1.95e-04
[C9] PASS shock is false only where the deck has the reconstruct section of that direction; otherwise it keeps the C++ default, true, and the density and pressure face floors do not run: no dynamics block: vertical True, horizontal True; no reconstruct block: vertical True, horizontal True; vertical only: vertical False, horizontal True; both sections: vertical False, horizontal False; shock set: vertical True, horizontal True. A reading of 'false by default from YAML' is wrong for 3 of 5 decks (no dynamics block, no reconstruct block, vertical only)
9/9 claims pass
